# IA Checklist

## 1. Purpose of This Checklist

This checklist helps students complete a final review before submitting the IBDP Computer Science IA.

It is designed to check whether the IA has a clear and connected project chain:

```text
problem → client/user needs → success criteria → design → development → testing → evaluation
```

::: tip Main Idea
A strong IA is not only a working product. It is a well-documented project with evidence, testing, and evaluation linked back to the original problem.
:::

---

## 2. How to Use This Checklist

Use this checklist in three stages:

```text
1. Before development
2. During development and testing
3. Before final submission
```

Do not wait until the final day.  
If a problem is found late, it may affect several sections.

For example:

```text
If success criteria are vague,
then testing becomes weak,
and evaluation becomes unsupported.
```

---

## 3. Overall IA Connection Check

Before checking each section, ask whether the whole IA feels connected.

| Question | Yes / No / Fix Needed |
|---|---|
| Is there a clear client/user? |  |
| Is the problem specific and realistic? |  |
| Are requirements based on client/user needs? |  |
| Are success criteria measurable? |  |
| Does the design support the criteria? |  |
| Does development show the criteria being implemented? |  |
| Does testing test the criteria? |  |
| Does evaluation judge the criteria? |  |
| Are limitations and improvements specific? |  |
| Does the final product solve the original problem? |  |

