### English Explanation

The IA checklist helps you check whether the whole IA forms a complete chain.

The most important thing is not whether one section is very long. The important thing is whether the sections connect:

```text
Problem Analysis explains the user's problem
Success Criteria define how success will be judged
Design plans how to implement the solution
Development shows how it was built
Testing proves whether it works
Evaluation judges whether the criteria were achieved
```

If a feature is mentioned early but is not designed, tested, or evaluated later, the IA feels disconnected.

For example:

```text
success criterion: user can search records
```

Then later, the IA should include:

```text
design: search screen / search algorithm
development: search code and explanation
testing: search tests
evaluation: whether search criterion was achieved
```

At the final check, do not only ask:

```text
Does my program run?
```

Also ask:

```text
Does my documentation prove why the product is needed?
Does it prove how it was built?
Does it prove whether it met the requirements?
Does it honestly explain limitations?
```

