## 6. Problem Analysis Checklist

### Client and User

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| The client is clearly identified. |  |
| The target user(s) are clearly identified. |  |
| The difference between client and user is clear if they are different. |  |
| The client/user has a realistic need. |  |
| The project is not just based on the student's personal interest. |  |

### Current System

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| The current method/system is described. |  |
| It explains who uses the current method. |  |
| It explains what data or information is currently used. |  |
| It explains how records are currently stored or managed. |  |
| It explains what is slow, difficult, inaccurate, or inconvenient. |  |

### Problem and Evidence

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| At least two specific problems are explained. |  |
| The problem is not described only as “bad” or “slow”. |  |
| Evidence from client/user or current method is included. |  |
| Private or sensitive information is removed or anonymized. |  |
| The need for a computer-based solution is justified. |  |

### Requirements, Constraints, and Scope

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Functional requirements are listed. |  |
| Non-functional requirements are considered where relevant. |  |
| Constraints are explained. |  |
| Project scope is realistic. |  |
| Out-of-scope features are explained if needed. |  |
| Requirements can lead naturally to success criteria. |  |

---

## 7. Success Criteria Checklist

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| There are usually 5-8 success criteria. |  |
| Each criterion links to a client/user need. |  |
| Each criterion is specific. |  |
| Each criterion is measurable. |  |
| Each criterion is testable. |  |
| Criteria are not only about appearance. |  |
| Criteria are not vague words such as “good”, “fast”, or “easy” without detail. |  |
| At least one criterion checks validation or error handling where relevant. |  |
| Data storage/retrieval is included if the product stores data. |  |
| Search/filter/sort/report features are included if they are core needs. |  |
| Each criterion can be evaluated as achieved, partly achieved, or not achieved. |  |

### Weak Criteria Warning

Rewrite criteria like:

```text
The system is useful.
The system looks good.
The system works well.
The system is easy to use.
The system is fast.
```

Make them measurable.

