## 9. Development Checklist

### Development Evidence

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Development is organized by feature or milestone. |  |
| Each major feature links to a success criterion. |  |
| Important code snippets are included. |  |
| Code snippets are explained in the student's own words. |  |
| Full code is not pasted unnecessarily in the main text. |  |
| Screenshots or output evidence are labelled. |  |
| Development evidence shows the product actually works. |  |

### Technical Explanation

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Algorithms are explained. |  |
| Data structures are explained. |  |
| File/database/storage handling is explained if used. |  |
| Validation and error handling are explained. |  |
| Search/filter/sort/calculation logic is explained if used. |  |
| The explanation includes input, processing, and output where relevant. |  |

### Problem Solving and Iteration

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| At least some development problems or bugs are discussed. |  |
| Fixes are explained. |  |
| Design changes are justified. |  |
| Prototype or client feedback influenced improvements if available. |  |
| The development process does not look like only a final screenshot collection. |  |

