## 10. Testing Checklist

### Test Table Quality

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Test cases are numbered. |  |
| Each test names the feature being tested. |  |
| Each test links to a success criterion where possible. |  |
| Exact test data is written. |  |
| Expected result is written before or clearly stated. |  |
| Actual result is recorded. |  |
| Pass/fail is shown. |  |
| Evidence is referenced. |  |
| Failed tests include fixes or retests where relevant. |  |

### Test Coverage

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Every success criterion is tested or evaluated. |  |
| Normal data is tested. |  |
| Invalid data is tested. |  |
| Boundary data is tested where relevant. |  |
| Validation is tested. |  |
| Storage/loading is tested if used. |  |
| Search/filter/sort/report features are tested if used. |  |
| User acceptance testing is included if possible. |  |
| Retesting is included after important fixes. |  |

### Evidence and Privacy

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Screenshots match the test cases. |  |
| Evidence is labelled clearly. |  |
| Private data is not exposed. |  |
| Sample/anonymized data is used where appropriate. |  |
| Evidence supports actual results. |  |

---

## 11. Evaluation Checklist

### Evaluation Against Criteria

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Every success criterion is evaluated. |  |
| Each criterion has evidence from testing. |  |
| Judgement is clear: achieved, partly achieved, or not achieved. |  |
| The explanation says why the judgement was made. |  |
| The evaluation does not simply repeat the testing table. |  |
| The evaluation connects back to the original problem. |  |

### Client/User Feedback

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Client/user feedback is included if possible. |  |
| Feedback is specific, not only “they liked it”. |  |
| Feedback is used to support evaluation. |  |
| Feedback also identifies possible improvements if available. |  |

### Limitations and Improvements

| Check | Done? |
|---|---|
| Specific limitations are identified. |  |
| Limitations are honest and realistic. |  |
| Future improvements link to limitations or feedback. |  |
| Improvements are realistic, not vague. |  |
| The final judgement explains whether the product solved the problem. |  |

