## 18. Common Final Submission Mistakes

| Mistake | Why It Hurts | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| final product changed after testing | tests may no longer prove final version | retest changed features |
| success criteria renumbered badly | references become confusing | update all references |
| screenshots not labelled | evidence hard to follow | label figures clearly |
| testing table has no actual results | incomplete testing | add actual result and pass/fail |
| evaluation has no evidence | unsupported claims | cite test/user evidence |
| final code not included | product evidence incomplete | attach appendix/code as required |
| client names/data exposed | privacy issue | anonymize sensitive data |
| too many screenshots, little explanation | weak analysis | explain what each evidence shows |
| improvements are vague | weak reflection | make them specific |
| no backup | submission risk | keep local/cloud backup |

